xgetopt (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Added 'getArgumentFor(shortopt)' method to OptionSequence class
    Returns a std::optional<std::string_view> containing either the argument
    for that option, or std::nullopt if that option was not provided, or did
    not come with an argument.
    This is not a breaking change.

 -- rail5 <andrew@rail5.org>  Thu, 21 May 2026 18:22:34 +0800

xgetopt (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bug fix: Respect explicit newlines in option descriptions
    Previously, these explicit newlines were mistakenly ignored.
    Added accompanying regression test.
  * Code style improvements:
    Use 'starts_with' instead of rfind
    Add copy/move constructors to FixedString internal helper class
    Restrict StopCondition to 8 bits
  * Added test for '-+'
    XGetOpt prepends a '+' character to the shortopt string to enforce
    POSIX-style parsing (REQUIRE_ORDER)
    Some getopt implementations may not support this (although so far
    every one tested does), in which case '+' would be treated as a normal
    option
    The new test case verifies that '+' is not treated as a normal
    option character (i.e., passing '-+' throws with 'unknown option')

 -- rail5 <andrew@rail5.org>  Thu, 26 Mar 2026 22:48:40 +0800

xgetopt (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * SemVer v1.0.0 release:
    + Commitment to long-term API stability
    + Guaranteed functionality on GNU platforms
      Support for other platforms is best-effort
      All tests passing on glibc, musl, OpenBSD, FreeBSD, macOS, and Haiku
  * Updates:
    + Compile-time guarantee: no two options in the same parser can share the
      same shortopt or the same longopt. This is done via static_assert
    + Added operator+ and operator+= to OptionSequence, allowing users to
      combine multiple OptionSequences into one (e.g. for repeated parsing)

 -- rail5 <andrew@rail5.org>  Fri, 13 Feb 2026 12:19:28 +0800

xgetopt (0.12.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Removed macros, instantiate via template programming
    The XGETOPT_PARSER and XGETOPT_OPTION macros have been removed.
    Users should now instantiate OptionParser directly using template
    parameters for each Option.
  * Compile-time guarantees: no duplicate short/long options within a single
    parser instance.
    If two options *in the same parser* share the same short or long option,
    a static_assert will trigger at compile-time.
    Without this, duplicate options would lead to undefined behavior at runtime
    when parsed by GNU getopt.

 -- rail5 <andrew@rail5.org>  Tue, 10 Feb 2026 08:52:39 +0800

